  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nA few showers or thunderstorms will be possible during the day \nThursday across far southeast Oklahoma as Edouard more or less \ndissipates over northern Texas. Meaningful rain amounts are not \nexpected, but at least a brief reprieve from the excessive heat \nis possible for locations south of I-40 as cloud cover becomes \nmore expansive Thursday. Better chances for excessive heat look \nto continue generally north of I-40 as higher cloud cover remains \nacross the south. Therefore, will issue another Heat Advisory for\nThursday afternoon across the north and into the Arkansas River\nValley. Beyond Thursday, persistence will be the theme of the \nforecast through the extended periods. Excessive heat will likely \nbe the main impact through the upcoming holiday weekend with more \nheat headlines possible through the period. Isolated afternoon \nshower or storm chances will become possible within the terrain \nareas through the weekend, owing to an uptick in moisture \nstreaming northward from the tropics over far eastern Oklahoma and\nwestern Arkansas. Upper ridging expands back over the Southern \nPlains into early next week, with hot and dry trends continuing \nfor the foreseeable future. The ongoing drought conditions look to\nworsen through the period, with occasionally gusty winds \nworsening fire weather conditions at times.\n\nBowlan",
